@kgibm The `-v` syntax is `host_path:machine_path`, so `-v /tmp:/Users/kevin/Projects/` mounts host's `/tmp` (On MacOS it is a symlink) into the VM at that path. Not what you intended. Also, specifying any `-v` replaces the default mounts (`/Users:/Users`, etc.), so your home directory is no longer visible to the VM, forcing the client to tar everything instead.

Could you test from a dedicated directory (not ~) with fresh machine?

Also, does OneDrive or any other cloud sync tool still run on the system?
